        "original_id": "4d47c808-e01b-5369-bebe-f168dd025cd6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Luis Gianneo, Ariel Ramírez, Juan Carlos Zorzi, Virtú Maragno, Pedro Ignacio Calderón, Rodolfo Arizaga\n- Roles: composer, pianist, conductor, music educator, music director\n- Topics: Argentine folk music, music education\n\nFacts:\n- Luis Gianneo was an Argentine composer, pianist, and conductor who lived from 1897 to 1968.\n- Ariel Ramírez was an Argentine composer, pianist, and music director who lived from 4 September 1921 to 18 February 2010.\n- Luis Gianneo worked as a music educator and taught composers including Ariel Ramírez, Juan Carlos Zorzi, Virtú Maragno, Pedro Ignacio Calderón, and Rodolfo Arizaga.\n- Ariel Ramírez was considered a chief exponent of Argentine folk music and was noted for his iconic musical compositions.",
